 ## Configuration
 
 - API keys come from `process.env`, auto-loaded by `server/src/env.ts` from (in order) repo-root `.env`, the legacy `kady_agent/.env` if present, and `server/.env`. `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is optional when model access comes entirely from OAuth or Ollama; Fusion and server-side speech remain OpenRouter-only. Other knobs include `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, `DEFAULT_MODEL_PROVIDER`, `DEFAULT_MODEL_ID`, `KADY_PORT`, and `KADY_PROJECTS_ROOT`.
+- **Outbound proxy.** `server/src/http-proxy.ts` installs undici's `EnvHttpProxyAgent` as the global dispatcher at boot (`index.ts`, `isMain` block) when `HTTP_PROXY`/`HTTPS_PROXY` is set, and is a no-op otherwise. Node's fetch ignores those variables on its own (`NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY` is Node ≥ 24 and we support ≥ 22.19), and Pi's `configureHttpDispatcher` isn't in the package's public exports — so without this the lead agent bypassed a proxy that the child `pi` processes running subagents already honoured. Note undici tunnels with `CONNECT` even for `http://` targets.
 - Pi OAuth tokens default to `~/.kady/pi-agent/auth.json`. `KADY_PI_AGENT_DIR` relocates that app-scoped directory; an explicitly supplied `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` takes precedence and can intentionally share a standalone Pi directory. The value is inherited by child `pi` processes, so lead and subagents share one auth store.
 - Settings exposes API keys (`/credentials`) plus Pi subscription authentication (`/model-providers`, `/model-auth/flows`) for OpenAI Codex (ChatGPT Plus/Pro), Anthropic (Claude Pro/Max), GitHub Copilot, and xAI. OAuth browser/device/manual prompts are mediated by `server/src/agent/provider-auth.ts` and `server/src/api/model-providers.ts`. MCP servers, native web search (pi-web-access), and **durable Modal remote compute** (hybrid tools + per-chat selector + project Compute tab) are also implemented. Still **deferred** from the pre-Pi stack: provenance/manifests and the "Copy as Methods" export, citation verification, and first-party literature search (Paperclip) / document conversion.
 
